kes sense as the next tool to use.\n</think>\n\nget_dependency_graph  \nTo analyze potential communication issues between microservices, I will retrieve the service dependency graph from Jaeger. This will reveal how services interact and identify any broken links, latency spikes, or failed calls that could indicate faults in the architecture. The graph will help pinpoint if a service is unreachable or causing cascading failures.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "get_dependency_graph", "arguments": {"last_n_minutes": 10}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=348, prompt_tokens=3359, total_tokens=3707, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd40-e9d5-74f3-b55b-079c2687b9cf-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3359, 'output_tokens': 348, 'total_tokens': 3707}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='a8f0d8d7-ddc7-41e8-8259-a0570e6b10b6')]]
