l with a query that lists all metrics for the cart service could help identify the correct labels. Alternatively, they could try a more general query to see if any data is returned. If the query still returns nothing, it might indicate a problem with the metrics setup or the service not being properly monitored. \n\nIn the next step, the user should adjust the query to use the correct service name and labels. They might also need to check the Prometheus configuration to ensure that the cart service\'s metrics are being scraped correctly. If the metrics are there but the query isn\'t matching, adjusting the query to use the right labels will be key. \n\nSo, the next tool call should be to get_metrics again with a revised query that uses the correct service name and labels. Alternatively, they could first check the available metrics to understand the correct labels to use. But given the previous response, the service name in the query might be incorrect, so adjusting that is the immediate next step.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"query": "sum by (service) (rate(http_requests_total{job=\\"cart\\"} [5m])) > 100"}', 'name': 'get_metrics'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b80c8c061eec0bdd', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 581, 'prompt_tokens': 2659, 'total_tokens': 3240, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd40-2195-7740-82a9-ffa56212b813-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_metrics', 'args': {'query': 'sum by (service) (rate(http_requests_total{job="cart"} [5m])) > 100'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b80c8c061eec0bdd', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2659, 'output_tokens': 581, 'total_tokens': 3240}), ToolMessage(content='("{\'