h one, but the logs command can be run on a specific pod if the name is known. Alternatively, they could use `kubectl logs -f` to follow the logs in real-time, but since the user is in a thinking stage, they might first want to check existing logs.\n\nAnother possibility is to check the readiness probe configuration in the deployment YAML. If the readiness probe is set to check a specific endpoint or uses a command that's failing, that could be the root cause. However, the user might need to inspect the deployment's YAML to see the probe settings. But since they already described the deployment, maybe the logs are more immediate.\n\nGiven the previous steps and the trace data, the most direct next action is to check the logs of the cart pods for any errors related to readiness probes or Redis connectivity. That would help confirm if the service is failing to meet the readiness criteria due to internal issues or external dependencies.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs -n astronomy-shop -l app=cart"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-be2360c93f6d6f7e', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 521, 'prompt_tokens': 11371, 'total_tokens': 11892, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd41-33b9-7861-8e1d-a8fae5373284-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs -n astronomy-shop -l app=cart'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-be2360c93f6d6f7e', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 11371, 'output_tokens': 521, 'total_tokens': 11892}), ToolMessage(content='', id='3d2ff9d0-ddae-4b01-9741-c1619b292229', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-be2360c93f6d