_graph  \nTo analyze potential communication issues between microservices, I will retrieve the service dependency graph from Jaeger. This will reveal how services interact and identify any broken links, latency spikes, or failed calls that could indicate faults in the architecture. The graph will help pinpoint if a service is unreachable or causing cascading failures.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "get_dependency_graph", "arguments": {"last_n_minutes": 10}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 348, 'prompt_tokens': 3359, 'total_tokens': 3707, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd40-e9d5-74f3-b55b-079c2687b9cf-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3359, 'output_tokens': 348, 'total_tokens': 3707}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='a8f0d8d7-ddc7-41e8-8259-a0570e6b10b6'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user is trying to diagnose an issue in the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application, which is a microservices-based system. They've already taken some steps: they retrieved the list of services, checked metrics for the 'cart' service, looked at deployments and pods, and now they're getting the dependency graph.\n\nThe last tool call was to get the dependency graph with a 10-minute window. The response from that tool call wasn't provided, but the user is now in the thinking stage again. They need to choose the next tool. Let me check the available tools again. The tools include get_traces, get_services, get_operations, get_dependency_graph, get_metrics, exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd, and submit_tool.\n\nSinc