oints. But the available tools include exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd, so maybe using that to describe the service or check the endpoints. However, the user might need to use the get_services tool to list the services and their endpoints. \n\nWait, the get_services tool returns service names from Grafana, which might not include endpoint details. The user might need to use kubectl to get the endpoints for the services. But the available commands include exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd, so the next step would be to run a command like kubectl get endpoints for flagd and valkey-cart in the namespace. That would show if the endpoints are correctly set up and if there are any issues with the service discovery. \n\nSo the correct tool call here would be to use exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the command to get endpoints for flagd and valkey-cart in the astronomy-shop namespace. That would help determine if the services are properly exposing their endpoints, which the cart service relies on. If the endpoints are not correctly set, that could cause the 503 error even if the pods are running.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get endpoints -n astronomy-shop -l app=flagd,valkey-cart"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b18139f567f13deb', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 664, 'prompt_tokens': 11822, 'total_tokens': 12486, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd41-c4a7-7413-b7ca-3dc5fce970ee-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get endpoints -n astronomy-shop -l app=flagd,valkey-cart'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b18139f567f13deb', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage